# This directory opts back into git. The repository root ignores everything by default (`*` in the
# root `.gitignore`), so each package that holds source states what it tracks. Without this file the
# Pi extensions live only on disk and a fresh clone cannot build them.
#
# Kept deliberately narrow: only source, never a build output or a copied `node_modules`. The
# extensions are plain TypeScript loaded at runtime by Pi, so the source IS the artifact.
*
!*/
.*/

# Source and its manifest files.
!*.ts
!*.js
!*.json
!*.nix
!*.md
!.gitignore

# A path-loaded extension may ship its own runtime dependencies; that tree is a build input, not
# source, and Nix vendors it beside the source instead of committing it.
node_modules/
